\f0\b0\fs24 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf0 \cb3 I like problems that don't have an obvious screen at the end of them. Give me a bus network, a warehouse full of robots, or a support queue nobody wants to own, and I'll go find out how it actually works before I open Figma. I've spent the last decade doing that at 
\f1\b \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 Halcyon Transit
\f0\b0 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 , 
\f1\b \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 Tidewater Robotics
\f0\b0 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 , and a small Portland agency called 
\f1\b \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 Paperboat Studio
\f0\b0 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 , and the thing I'm proudest of is never being the designer who shipped the clean mockup that broke on day one.\cb1 \
\cb3 These days I lead design for Halcyon's rider app and the operator tools that keep it running, which means I split my time between people riding the bus and people driving it. I write code when it gets an idea in front of engineering faster, I run my own research, and I'd rather ship something rough and true than something polished and wrong. If you want a designer who reads the support tickets, that's me.\cb1 \
